# RVM-minted trade domains for the 60-trade catalogue (CEO pack v2, ruled 2026-11-23; #3007).
#
# Pack section 13.2: India's occupation list (NCO-2015) has no entry for a CMM operator, an NDT
# technician or a piping designer. A form's family must bind to an occupation and a phrase must
# point at one, so these three are minted here under the `jd_rvm_<slug>` rule, in the shape of
# rvm-3d-cad-design.jsonl. Pack rule 13.3.2: these three only. The other "partial gap" trades
# (wire-cut EDM, CNC grinding, powder coating, laser cutting, tube bending, PLC programmer, ...)
# each already have at least one bound NCO code and get no minted entry.
#
# Parents:
#   CMM, NDT  -> ISCO 7543 Product Graders and Testers. NOT 3211.0100 "X-Ray Technician" for NDT:
#               that code is medical.
#   Piping    -> ISCO 3118 Draughtspersons, the same parent as the 3D CAD designer.
#
# Each entry carries one alias, the trade's plain English name, so it is visible to search. The
# full phrase sets arrive with the waves (#3010 Wave 1 for T33 CMM, #3016 for T34 NDT, #3017 for
# T60 Piping); the family bindings arrive with the forms (#3008, #3016, #3017). Until then the
# entries resolve through their unit group like any unbound code. label_hi is null: no Devanagari
# is signed for these names yet (#3018).
